  abstract = {Based on a generalization of the Hilfer--Katugampola fractional operator, recently introduced, and the Weyl fractional derivative, which are responsible for describing memory and distance effects, respectively, we investigate anomalous diffusion in processes in which a fractional radial differential equation plays an important and fundamental role. Similarity solutions for this fractional space--time radial equation are considered. These solutions are presented in terms of the Fox's H-function. As an application, we present and discuss a special case in fractal Hausdorff dimension.},
