  keywords = {Gaussian processes, hierarchical matrices, matrix-free methods, spatial statistics, large-scale spatial modeling},
  abstract = {Gaussian processes are essential for spatial data analysis and uncertainty quantification, but dense matrix operations make direct computation infeasible at large scale. This article proposes smashGP, a framework that uses hierarchical matrices and matrix-free methods to exploit kernel structure in Gaussian process covariance matrices. The approach supports fast matrix-vector products, likelihood approximation, prediction, and uncertainty quantification for large spatial datasets, and can be parallelized on shared-memory systems. Simulations and case studies illustrate its advantages over competing scalable Gaussian process methods.},
